# The Debian packages later stages install on the base root, pinned so every consumer
# takes the same archives. `bun src/container.ts pin-inputs` pins each one and its
# closure beyond the floor in locks/upstream.lock, selected in locks/packages.tsv as
# upstream-<root> for the roots that need it; they are never installed into the base
# root and are published as the upstream rows of the release's mica-system-base.lock.
#
# A later stage may take any upstream row of the release by its package name: every
# row's dependencies are rows too, or in the floor. A package the lock does not pin at
# all is added under options.

# The init a product chooses. systemd: mica-systemd's Debian half.
systemd
systemd-sysv
udev
systemd-resolved
systemd-timesyncd
systemd-repart
# OpenRC: mica-openrc's Debian half.
openrc
fdisk

# options: what boards, engines and products add beside the floor.
alsa-utils
bash
bluez
coreutils
diffutils
dmsetup
dropbear-bin
findutils
grep
gzip
iw
kmod
libasound2t64
libatomic1
libdw1t64
libglib2.0-0t64
libjson-c5
libnl-genl-3-200
libreadline8t64
libseccomp2
libssl3t64
libsubid5
login
nftables
procps
readline-common
rfkill
sed
